# Ciyahi website — project context

Full handover doc: **`HANDOVER.md`** at the repo root. Read it before starting non-trivial work — it has
the site map, the design-system component catalog, and the reasoning behind recent structural decisions.
This file is the condensed version that's always in context.

## What this is
Marketing site for Ciyahi Limited (enterprise AI implementation company, flagship product InvoAIce.io —
AP automation, live in production). React 19 + Vite 8 + React Router v7, no backend, content lives in JS
arrays inside page components. Dev server: `npm run dev` (port 5173) — keep it running and verify visual
changes in the browser, this is a design-sensitive marketing site.

## Hard guardrails — do not violate these without explicit user instruction

1. **No client names anywhere.** The one detailed case study (`/document-intelligence`, an insurance
   document-intake + submission-to-quote pipeline) refers only to "an insurance brokerage" / "insurance
   brokerages running real-estate consortium programs."
2. **Risk modeling and pricing engines in that case study are third-party systems Ciyahi integrated
   with — Ciyahi did NOT build them.** Copy must say things like "auto-submitted to the firm's risk
   modeling and pricing systems," never "we built/run the risk model." This was an explicit correction
   from the client — don't regress it.
3. **Ateequeullah Khan is Non-Executive Director & Co-Founder** (H-1B visa constraint — he cannot hold an
   active officer title in the US entity). Iqbal Shaikh is the active Director/CEO and is listed first.
   Don't change either title without being told to.
4. **Don't reintroduce old positioning**: this site used to be finance-automation-only and used DM Serif
   Display for headings. Both were deliberately replaced with a broader "enterprise AI, any domain"
   positioning and Space Grotesk headings. Don't drift back.
5. **`/services` (generic capabilities) and `/use-cases` (concrete delivered proof) are intentionally
   separate pages.** Don't merge the detailed case-study content back into the Services page — that was
   tried and explicitly reverted for being bloated. Services links out to Use Cases via the compact
   `.promo-banner` component instead.

## Design system — reuse before inventing
`src/styles/style.css` has the full component catalog. Key reusable pieces, see HANDOVER.md §6 for
details: `.hero` (dark drifting gradient + `.hero-cycle` rotating headline word), `.orbit` (animated
system diagram), magnetic-tilt on `.svc-tile` (mouse-tracked 3D card tilt, driven from a `useEffect` in
`Home.jsx`), `.pipe` (animated flowing-light pipeline/timeline), `.app-window` (fake product-UI mockup
for "show, don't tell"), `.promo-banner` (compact callout linking to deeper content), `.featured-svc`
(large dark story block — currently only on `/document-intelligence`, don't duplicate elsewhere).

## Copy style
Short. Tile/card descriptions are one tight sentence. Long-form prose belongs on deep-dive pages like
`/document-intelligence`, not on listing pages.

